{
 "source": "trapp",
 "book": "1CH",
 "chapter": 9,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.1",
   "range": "1CH.9.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a4341c65",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.1#p1-a4341c65",
     "text": "Not now extant. This chapter, and 1Ch 3:19; 1Ch 3:24, are noted for some parcels of the last passages, for history, of the Old Testament.",
     "anchor": "In the book of the kings.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ch 3:19",
       "ref": "1CH.3.19"
      },
      {
       "text": "1Ch 3:24",
       "ref": "1CH.3.24"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.2",
   "range": "1CH.9.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "adb65e71",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.2#p1-f74fb27e",
     "text": "sc., After the return from captivity. {Ezr 1:1-11; Ezr 2:1-60}",
     "anchor": "Now the first inhabitants",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Ezr 1:1-11",
       "ref": "EZR.1.1-11"
      },
      {
       "text": "Ezr 2:1-60",
       "ref": "EZR.2.1-60"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.2#p2-d5b86de9",
     "text": "The same they had before the captivity. A wonderful providence of God it was, that as the land kept her Sabbaths for those seventy years, so the country should be all that while kept empty, till the return of the natives: for we read not that any colonies were sent thither, nor any displaced to make room for these at their return.",
     "anchor": "That dwelt in their possessions."
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.2#p3-8961f5ab",
     "text": "Dedititii; these were the posterity of those old Gibeonites. {Jos 9:3-17} {See Trapp on \"Ezr 2:58\"} Vocati ad vilia officia Deum respiciant, &c. {a}",
     "anchor": "And the Nethinims.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Jos 9:3-17",
       "ref": "JOS.9.3-17"
      },
      {
       "text": "Ezr 2:58",
       "ref": "EZR.2.58"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.2#p4-1ebd8d0e",
     "text": "{a} Lavat."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.3",
   "range": "1CH.9.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1e12df99",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.3#p1-1e12df99",
     "text": "See Neh 11:1-2.",
     "anchor": "And in Jerusalem dwelt.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Neh 11:1-2",
       "ref": "NEH.11.1-2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.4",
   "range": "1CH.9.4",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d3706039",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.4#p1-d3706039",
     "text": "See the same catalogue in Neh 11:4-36, though with some alteration of names, as before often.",
     "anchor": "Uthai, &c.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Neh 11:4-36",
       "ref": "NEH.11.4-36"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.5",
   "range": "1CH.9.5",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "09ec2476",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.5#p1-caba1776",
     "text": "The posterity of Shelah, son of Judah. {a} {Gen 38:5}",
     "anchor": "And the Shilonites.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Gen 38:5",
       "ref": "GEN.38.5"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.5#p2-6187fce6",
     "text": "{a} A Lapide."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.7",
   "range": "1CH.9.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "912831da",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.7#p1-912831da",
     "text": "Alias Joed. {Neh 11:7} Names are oft abbreviated.",
     "anchor": "Hodaviah.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Neh 11:7",
       "ref": "NEH.11.7"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.10",
   "range": "1CH.9.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b9f05542",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.10#p1-b9f05542",
     "text": "He had reckoned four distinct orders or ranks of people among the Jews, {1Ch 9:2} and here he instanceth the second order or classis; viz., Sacerdotalis: Priestly.",
     "anchor": "And of the priests.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ch 9:2",
       "ref": "1CH.9.2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.11",
   "range": "1CH.9.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6ba697c6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.11#p1-6badc482",
     "text": "Who found the book of the law, which was presented to Josiah. {2Ki 22:8-10}",
     "anchor": "The son of Hilkiah.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Ki 22:8-10",
       "ref": "2KI.22.8-10"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.11#p2-6df4cdaa",
     "text": "Next to the high priest.",
     "anchor": "The ruler of the house of God."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.13",
   "range": "1CH.9.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b90de8fd",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.13#p1-b90de8fd",
     "text": "Or, Men of work for the service, &c., that is, able and apt for the work.",
     "anchor": "For the work of the service."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.14",
   "range": "1CH.9.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "08bb7391",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.14#p1-08bb7391",
     "text": "See 1Ch 9:2; 1Ch 9:10.",
     "anchor": "And of the Levites.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ch 9:2",
       "ref": "1CH.9.2"
      },
      {
       "text": "1Ch 9:10",
       "ref": "1CH.9.10"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.15",
   "range": "1CH.9.15",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e76e0763",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.15#p1-e76e0763",
     "text": "Which Asaph is said to be the principal to begin the thanksgiving in prayer. {Neh 11:17} {See Trapp on \"Neh 11:17\"}",
     "anchor": "The son of Asaph.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Neh 11:17",
       "ref": "NEH.11.17"
      },
      {
       "text": "Neh 11:17",
       "ref": "NEH.11.17"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.17",
   "range": "1CH.9.17",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "db07fe22",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.17#p1-db07fe22",
     "text": "He was overseer of the overseers of the porters.",
     "anchor": "Shallum was the chief."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.18",
   "range": "1CH.9.18",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1ae751ca",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.18#p1-1ae751ca",
     "text": "Even till the time that this book was gathered out of the ancient chronicles. {1Ch 9:1}",
     "anchor": "Who hitherto.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ch 9:1",
       "ref": "1CH.9.1"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.19",
   "range": "1CH.9.19",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "8330c67c",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.19#p1-8330c67c",
     "text": "viz, When they of old encamped round about the tabernacle, in the wilderness.",
     "anchor": "Being over the host of the Lord"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.20",
   "range": "1CH.9.20",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "66788043",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.20#p1-66788043",
     "text": "To assist and accept him in his generous actions.",
     "anchor": "And the Lord was with him."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.22",
   "range": "1CH.9.22",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "f9b060e3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.22#p1-f9b060e3",
     "text": "Or, For their fidelity. Or, In their trust, committed unto them by God and the commonwealth.",
     "anchor": "In their set office."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.23",
   "range": "1CH.9.23",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "adf72935",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.23#p1-adf72935",
     "text": "i.e., By three distinct courses. {1Ch 9:25}",
     "anchor": "By wards",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ch 9:25",
       "ref": "1CH.9.25"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.24",
   "range": "1CH.9.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7856b1b6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.24#p1-7856b1b6",
     "text": "The four parts of the temple answered to the four parts of the world. on Mat 8:11.",
     "anchor": "Towards the east.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 8:11",
       "ref": "MAT.8.11"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.33",
   "range": "1CH.9.33",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4fa07299",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.33#p1-4fa07299",
     "text": "i.e., Freed from all other employments.",
     "anchor": "Were free"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.35",
   "range": "1CH.9.35",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "9961426d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.35#p1-9961426d",
     "text": "Saul’s race is here reiterated for some unknown cause, saith Diodate; for a preparation to the ensuing history, say others."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.9.44",
   "range": "1CH.9.44",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "035bab71",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.9.44#p1-035bab71",
     "text": "And here end the genealogies; the history followeth, and chiefly of David, in praise of whom this First Book of Chronicles, was especially written, as Vatablus observeth.",
     "anchor": "These were the sons of Azel."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
